        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl lg:text-4xl text-ink leading-tight mb-5">Psychological Support for University Students in Famagusta: A Complete Guide</h1>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-lg leading-relaxed">University years can be both exciting and deeply challenging. Exam pressure, dormitory life, homesickness, the search for identity — these are normal feelings, but sometimes you need professional support. This guide clarifies the options available to you in Famagusta.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-12 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <div class="prose-custom space-y-8">

          <div>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Famagusta welcomes university students from more than 100 countries. That diversity enriches campus life, but it also means each student faces a unique set of challenges around adjustment and academic pressure. Knowing where to turn when things get hard makes a real difference.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Why do students' mental health often suffer at university?</h2>
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Adjustment difficulties in a new environment</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Leaving family for the first time, starting out in an unfamiliar city or country, building new friendships — combined, these create a heavy adjustment burden.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Academic pressure</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Midterms, finals, project deadlines and grade anxiety — especially when a scholarship or visa depends on academic performance — can tip into chronic stress.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Loneliness and homesickness</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Social media exaggerates how much fun everyone else is having. Meanwhile, you may be sitting alone in your dorm room. That contradiction deepens homesickness and low mood.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Identity and uncertainty about the future</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Regret about your choice of degree, career uncertainty, wrestling with "who am I?" — the existential questions that surface at university carry real psychological weight.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">Seeing a psychologist does not mean you are "crazy"</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">This stigma still stops many students from seeking support. Yet therapy is an evidence-based form of support for everyday challenges such as adjustment difficulties, anxiety, low motivation and relationship issues. Asking for help is a sign of strength, not weakness.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Exam nerves or an anxiety disorder?</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Feeling tense before an exam is normal and can even improve performance. But if the following symptoms become persistent, speaking to a psychologist is worth considering:</p>
            <ul class="space-y-2">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">A constant anxiety that doesn't lift, even outside exam periods</p>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Sleep disturbances, changes in appetite or difficulty concentrating</p>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Avoiding social situations or not wanting to go outside</p>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Unable to attend lectures or complete assignments</p>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">A constant urge to cry, or emotional numbness</p>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Support at Famagusta Psychology Centre</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Famagusta Psychology Centre offers flexible appointment times to fit around busy study schedules, with student-friendly pricing. Sessions are available in both English and Turkish, making the service accessible to international students as well as local ones.</p>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">What we offer students</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Exam anxiety and academic stress</li>
                  <li>• Adjustment difficulties and homesickness</li>
                  <li>• Identity and career uncertainty</li>
                  <li>• Relationship difficulties</li>
                  <li>• Online session option</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Practical details</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Sessions in English &amp; Turkish</li>
                  <li>• Morning, midday and evening slots</li>
                  <li>• Full confidentiality guaranteed</li>
                  <li>• Easy booking via WhatsApp</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Why are online sessions particularly useful for students?</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">During exam periods time is tight, and your dorm or accommodation may be far from the centre. Online sessions remove these barriers: you can have a session before a lecture or in the early evening, from your own space, via a secure video connection.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Research confirms that online therapy is as effective as face-to-face therapy. Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (CBT) for anxiety and depression, in particular, works just as well online as it does in person.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-accent/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-accent/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">Do not wait until things reach a crisis</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Most students wait until things get worse. But therapy is most effective — and takes the shortest time — when problems are addressed early, before they deepen. If something feels wrong, that is reason enough.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
